WHEREAS the E1 – South Orléans-Wall Road Lands comprise approximately 288 hectares of greenfield and are anticipated to accommodate a significant new community with thousands of future residents;
AND WHEREAS the planning of a new community of this scale requires careful coordinated consideration of transportation, servicing, parks, schools, stormwater management, active transportation, and other supporting infrastructure to ensure complete and sustainable community design;
AND WHEREAS a Secondary Plan provides the appropriate comprehensive planning framework and opportunities for meaningful public consultation to guide the long-term development of a community of this size and complexity;
THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED that Recommendation 2 be amended by deleting the words "and E1 – South Orléans-Wall Road Lands".

WHEREAS on November 9, 2022 City Council passed By-law 2022-377 which rezoned a strip, 20 metres in width or less, of part of the lands addressed as 1 and 7 Cheryl Road and part of 5  Majestic Drive from R3WW to R3WW[2842], prohibiting development on the said strip of land to protect lands potentially required for Barrhaven Light Rail Transit (“LRT”) infrastructure, pending design work to be completed as part of an Environmental Assessment (“EA”);
AND WHEREAS the Omnibus Zoning By-law Amendment Report proposes to reintroduce the By-law 2022-377 amendment on those lands, which has not yet been carried forward into the new, 2026 Zoning By-law;
AND WHEREAS at the time By-law 2022-377 was passed, the available design work had not confirmed the extent of the property requirement to accommodate the Barrhaven LRT facility.
AND WHEREAS the EA study was approved by Council on May 10, 2023 and is now referenced in Schedule C16 of the City of Ottawa Official Plan;
AND WHERAS the completed EA study identifies that only a small amount of the lands affected by Zoning By-law Amendment 2022-377 will be required for the Barrhaven LRT project;
AND WHEREAS By-law 2022-377 was appealed by the landowners and remains under appeal and no notice of a by-law to repeal a zoning by-law which is under appeal is required pursuant to thePlanning Act;
THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED that the following changes be made to the Staff Report:
THEREFORE BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED that Planning and Housing Committee recommend that Council repeal By-law 2022-377.
